---
# This file has to exist whatever it contains, and that is separate from what it now says.
#
# Why it must exist: servicesFromKubernetes() calls checkAndCopyConfig("kubernetes.yaml") on
# EVERY service/widget lookup (service-helpers.js, via getServiceItem's docker/kubernetes
# discovery fallback — unconditional, not gated on any service actually using a kubernetes:
# widget). checkAndCopyConfig only copies its skeleton when the file is missing; against a
# read-only mount that copy fails with EROFS and the app calls process.exit(1) — a crash loop
# on the very first widget poll. Since E3 the config lives on a writable emptyDir seeded from
# the Secret, so this is no longer the crash it once was, but the file stays declared here so
# our content wins over whatever skeleton the image would seed.
#
# What it says: `cluster` mode makes homepage authenticate to the API with the pod's mounted
# ServiceAccount — the one rbac.yaml.j2 creates and deployment.yaml.j2 names. That backs both
# the kubernetes info widget (cluster/node CPU + memory) and the per-tile pod stats in
# services.yaml. No `ingress:`/`traefik:`/`gateway:` keys: homepage's automatic service
# DISCOVERY stays off, because every tile here is hand-authored and a discovered duplicate of
# one is worse than no tile at all.
mode: cluster
